KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ cast __integer_pack yields \{0,1\}: 0\+1==1: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG must FAIL: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
--
KNOWNBUG: the GCC `__integer_pack` builtin with a CAST argument, as libstdc++
writes std::make_integer_sequence (`integer_sequence<T, __integer_pack(T(N))...>`,
note the `T(N)` cast).  The direct form `__integer_pack(N)...` is handled
(cpp17_integer_pack_builtin, CORE); the cast form is resolved eagerly during the
alias body substitution and never reaches the typecheck_template_args expansion,
so CBMC rejects `__integer_pack` and leaves the body incomplete -> VERIFICATION
SUCCESSFUL vacuously (does NOT match the desc above, so a known bug).  This is the
remaining cpp17_apply_basic blocker (std::apply deduces its __apply_impl
index_sequence from a make_index_sequence value).  __integer_pack is GCC-only;
g++ runs r == 1.  When the cast form is expanded, assertion 2 fails and the desc
matches (promote to CORE).
